AMIN D. BROOKER Junior (Benjamin1), birth c1790 or 1797 (implied by age at death).  First death report died 08 Jul 1837, Scituate, age 47 (handwritten); buried “city poor,” South Burial Ground, Boston, Suffolk County. Second death report, died 07 Jul 1837, City of Boston, age “about 40” (typed), same burial information. Either age is plausible.
First marriage intention published 14 Feb 1813, Beverly, Essex County; married 02 Jul 1815, Boston, performed by Thomas Baldwin, to Olive “Olley” Russell,,, daughter of Caesar Russell (as “Rusel”) and Sarah Richardson, birth 22 Apr 1792, Beverly. (This same pastor married Benjamin’s brother to Olley’s sister three years later.)
Second marriage intention published 05 Oct 1834, Scituate, to Alice Lee (widow of David Tue, also listed as Tew), daughter of Jupiter Lee, another Forgotten Patriot (a Fatigueman; stationed at West Point in the NY Northern Department);

